// Regression: a tuplet on ONE staff must not break another staff's beaming.
// Upper staff has a quarter-note triplet; lower staff has eight straight eighths
// that must beam 4+4. Auto-beaming breaks at a tuplet boundary by note index, so
// a per-staff beam pass must see only its OWN staff's tuplets — else the upper
// triplet's end-index splits the lower staff's first beam group ([c d] + two stray
// flags + [g a b c']). Tuplets carry a StaffIndex; the beam pass now filters by it.
// LILYPOND-REF: lily/auto-beam-engraver.cc — beaming is per Voice/Staff context.
octave absolute
title "Multi-staff tuplet + beams"
part rh { clef treble }
part lh { clef bass }
section S {
  rh { tuplet 3/2 { c''4 c'' c'' } c''2 | }
  lh { c8 d e f g a b c' | }
}
structure { S }
score "multistaff-tuplet-beams" { grandStaff { staff rh staff lh } }
